<a name="english"></a>
SIT∞ — Stateless Process Engine (English)

A deterministic pure-JavaScript engine that regenerates content from a generative law (seed + frequency bank of real Riemann-zeta zero ordinates), without storing data matrices or state histories.

Honest scope: stateless rendering and deterministic replay are real (bit-exact verified). Arbitrary data still requires storage (Kolmogórov incompressibility); the demo measures the true residue (~99.7% on random bytes). No claim is made about solving Riemann's Hypothesis or Gödel's theorems — they are bypassed, not refuted. The Riemann zeros are used strictly as a frequency bank.

Known limitations: O(N) replay cost (mitigated by sealed phase anchors), bit-exactness only verified on V8/Chromium doubles, hardcoded 10-zero bank.

Formal Mathematics of SOR (extracted from technical documentation):

    Belnap-Dunn Matrix: SOR introduces [N] None and [B] Both states to dissolve paradoxes without blocking memory.

    1/0 as Distribution Operator (E/S(1:M)): A single ray enters the membrane and unfolds into a continuous harmonic spectrum.

    O(1) Memory and Euler's Pentavariable Identity: Phase difference collapses to unity (n^1 - (n-1) = 1), guaranteeing constant storage cost regardless of input scale.

